<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Contract

`<<~ kumu Name props>>` … `<<~/kumu>>` DECLARES a named structural node type — a reusable container shape. `sigil-kumu.tid` carries it with `lar-kind: pragma` and `lar-render: compile`: the declaration registers the type and emits no render output of its own.

''Kumu declares a type; wehe declares a procedure.'' The two pragmas sit side by side and answer different questions.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/resolution>>

!! How a Declaration Reaches a Placement

A kumu definition tiddler wears the tag `lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/kumu` and carries its name in the `kumu-name` field. `~kau` resolves a placement against exactly that pair:

```
[all[tiddlers+shadows]tag[lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/kumu]field:kumu-name<_kau-name>first[]else[]]
```

An unresolved name renders `<span class="lar-kau-hole">` at the placement site, so a device nobody declared reads as a hole rather than as silence.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/source>>

